            <section class="p2 heading white no-bottom-padding">
         <div class="wrap text-left">
         <h1 class="heading">The Historic Grand Theater</h1>
         </div>
        </section>
            <section class="p2 body-text white">
            <div class="wrap column-1">
                                <div class=" no-break"> 
                                        <p>Gray Area is located in the historic Grand Theater, built in 1940. We offer modern sound, light, and visual capabilities, fiber internet, and full bar packages. The 10,000 square foot San Francisco landmark is a versatile venue available for performances, conferences, and exhibitions. </p>
                    </div>
                            </div>
        </section>
            <section class="p2 full-width-image">

            <div class="image" style="background-image:url(https://grayarea.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/grand-theater-historical.jpg)">
                <span role="img" aria-label=""> </span>
                                    <div class="caption"><div class="wrap">2665 Mission Street, c. 1970</div></div>
                            </div>

        </section>
            <section class="p2 heading white no-bottom-padding">
         <div class="wrap text-left">
         <h4 class="heading">Are you a nonprofit 501(c)3 organization?</h4>
         </div>
        </section>
            <section class="p2 body-text white">
            <div class="wrap column-1">
                                <div class=" no-break"> 
                                            <h5 class="bold">Community Partnership Rental Program</h5>
                                        <p>Gray Area is proud to offer a community rentals program to organizations with nonprofit 501(c)3 status to leverage our space for community support and social good. Events or organizations that qualify for this program must satisfy one or more of the following program goals:</p>
<p>1) to serve the local Mission District community<br />
2) to elevate and organize around issues of social justice<br />
3) to support, or increase visibility of, underserved communities<br />
4) to advance under-supported fields in the arts and/or in technology</p>
<p>Benefits of the community rentals program include listing on the Gray Area website, digital marketing, and discounted gear and rental fees. Past program recipients include: <a href="http://www.missionculturalcenter.org/">Mission Cultural Center</a>, <a href="http://eltecolote.org/content/en/">El Tecolote</a>, <a href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/LetsTakeActionSF/">Let's Take Action</a>, <a href="http://www.dawsondancesf.org/">Dawson Dance SF</a>, <a href="http://counterpulse.org/">CounterPulse</a>, <a herf="https://www.cca.edu/">CCA</a>, <a href="https://www.bavc.org/">BAVC</a>, and more.</p>
                    </div>
                            </div>
        </section>
            <section class="p2 white">
            <div class="wrap text-center">
                                    <a class="button color-4 button-large" href="https://airtable.com/appHZcmX68z1AwtEE/pagBWd7oBGvByR5Vq/form">Community Rental Form</a>
                            </div>
        </section>
            <section class="p2 body-text white">
            <div class="wrap column-1">
                                <div class=" no-break"> 
                                            <h5 class="bold">COVID-19 Updates</h5>
                                        <p>Our team is working hard to keep a safe environment:<br />
• Intimate: Restricted capacity to allow for social distancing.<br />
• Air Circulation: New increased ventilation in the lobby and performance space.<br />
• Cleanliness: New enhanced cleaning policy; we are fully sanitizing the entire facility every day and providing hand sanitizer. </p>
<p><i>* Please note any interaction with the general public poses an elevated risk of being exposed to COVID-19 and we cannot guarantee that you will not be exposed while in attendance at the event. We are following state and federal guidance, and doing everything we can to minimize risk to our guests.</i></p>
                    </div>
                            </div>
        </section>
    
